# Environment examples for HiveOS v0.1. NEVER commit real .env files (ADR-022).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A) infrastructure/.env (local DEV compose; copy beside this name)
#    used by docker-compose.yml (review R3-1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# POSTGRES_USER=hiveos
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
# POSTGRES_DB=hiveos
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5434
# URL the api container uses to reach the db service inside compose:
# HIVEOS_DEV_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://hiveos:change-me@db:5432/hiveos

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# B) /opt/hiveos/app/.env (SERVER; staging/prod)
#    remote-deploy.sh REGENERATES this file each deploy:
#    IMAGE_TAG + DATABASE_URL (password from /opt/hiveos/secrets/pg_password,
#    host = "db" service DNS via external network hiveos_default).
#    ENVIRONMENT may be preset in /etc/environment or passed inline.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# IMAGE_TAG=dev-local
# ENVIRONMENT=staging
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://hiveos:CHANGE_ME@db:5432/hiveos
